  <h2>What this is</h2>
  <p>
    Testosterone decline in men begins gradually in the early 30s and accelerates with
    poor sleep, excess body fat, chronic stress, and environmental exposures. Most men
    don't connect the dots — the fatigue, the mood flatness, the lost motivation, the
    slower recovery — until the numbers are already significantly off.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Muscle pillar incorporates hormone optimization as a foundational layer because
    no training or nutrition protocol reaches its full potential in a hormonally depleted
    environment. We partner with a licensed telemedicine practice for men who are appropriate
    candidates for testosterone replacement therapy or related hormone protocols.
  </p>

  <h2>Our approach</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Hormone Panel Baseline</h3>
      <p>Total T, free T, SHBG, LH, estradiol, and metabolic markers — not just one number.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Lifestyle Foundation First</h3>
      <p>Sleep, zinc, vitamin D, and body fat optimization often move the needle significantly before any therapy is considered.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>TRT Telemedicine Lane</h3>
      <p>Our contracted telemedicine partner evaluates and manages TRT for clinically appropriate candidates.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Ongoing Monitoring</h3>
      <p>Quarterly labs and protocol adjustments — hormones are a moving target, not a one-time fix.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

